# {{App}}

Generated by [DotNetArch](https://github.com/moein-rezaee/DotNetArch) (layout v2): Clean Architecture, ports and adapters,
vertical slices with CQRS (MediatR), unit of work and repository.

## Purpose
Describe in two sentences what this service owns and who calls it (`docs/specs/overview.md` has the detail).

## Scope
The service and its repository only. Other services are reached through ports and adapters.

## Prerequisites
.NET SDK (see `global.json`), a database (see `DATABASE_CONNECTION_STRING`), and the packages of the feed in `NuGet.config`.

## Layout
```text
src/
  {{App}}.Domain           entities, value objects, domain events (no references)
  {{App}}.Application      ports (interfaces), features/<entities>/{Commands,Queries,Actions,Events,Dtos}, validators
  {{App}}.Infrastructure   EF Core persistence, repositories, unit of work, adapters for ports
  {{App}}.Api              controllers, configuration, composition root
```
Dependencies point inwards: `Api -> Infrastructure -> Application -> Domain`. Each layer registers its own services
(`AddApplication`, `AddInfrastructure`, `AddApi`).

## Configuration
- `appsettings.json` - non-sensitive settings (`Database:Provider`, `Cors:AllowedOrigins`, logging).
- `.env` / environment variables - secrets and run-time values (`DATABASE_CONNECTION_STRING`). Real environment variables win over `.env`.
- Keep `.env.example` and `appsettings.example.json` in sync with the code.

## Run / Usage
```bash
cp src/{{App}}.Api/.env.example src/{{App}}.Api/.env   # secrets and run-time values
dotnet run --project src/{{App}}.Api
```

Generate more with the tool:
```bash
dotnet-arch new crud --entity=Product
dotnet-arch new action --entity=Product --method=POST --action=Archive
```

## Validation / Verification
`dotnet build -c Release` is warning-free, `dotnet test` passes, and `dotnet-arch doctor` has no finding.

## Troubleshooting
`dotnet-arch doctor` names the rule and the file; `dotnet-arch fix` repairs what is mechanical. A missing `DATABASE_CONNECTION_STRING` stops the start with a message naming the key.

